<title>BELGIUM: EU takes 27,051 tns beef into intervention.</title>
<headline>EU takes 27,051 tns beef into intervention.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's beef management committee accepted bids for 27,051 tonnes of beef into intervention stores on Friday, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The bids were accepted at a maximum price of 261 ecus per 100 kg,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The total included 1,559 tonnes of young French store cattle following the collapse of the traditional French summer trade to Italy because of public concen about mad cow disease, the official added.</p>
<p>The store cattle price was fixed at 126 percent of the 261 ecus per 100 kg for category A and C beef.</p>
</text>
